OL,3,ARussia's own figures show it has lost  
OL,4,Anearly 500,000 people in Ukraine war   
OL,6,FAt least 490,334 Russian soldiers have 
OL,7,Fdied since the start of the war in     
OL,8,FUkraine in 2022, according to Russian  
OL,9,Fgovernment statistics analysed by the  
OL,10,FBBC.                                   
OL,12,FThe leaked Rosstat data reveal how the 
OL,13,Ffull-scale invasion of Ukraine has     
OL,14,Ffundamentally changed mortality        
OL,15,Fpatterns in Russia, and show the high  
OL,16,Fcost paid in human life in a war that  
OL,17,FVladimir Putin had assumed would last  
OL,18,Fonly days but is now almost five years 
OL,19,Fold.                                   
